    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0238" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/4826: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bucknell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-02">December 2,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7616. Your 8402, 2d. Procedure outlined is very agreeable to us. A statement
                    which can mutually be modified in phraseology to some extent to meet our
                    respective needs would seem to be a very practical solution and could be used
                    here in connection with the statement Long made to the House Committee<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d199-f1"/> as it could be used there as basis for statement
                    to Parliament. Your close attention to this matter is appreciated and is
                    entirely justified by the importance which it assumes here from the point of
                    view of public interest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d199-f1" n="11" xml:id="d199-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Rescue of the Jewish and Other Peoples in Nazi-Occupied
